## Commands

```bash
make install   # uv venv + editable install with the "[[ test_extras ]]" extras
make test      # pytest --tb=short -q
make lint      # ruff check + format --check[[ (' (pinned ruff ' ~ ruff_pin ~ ')') if ruff_pin else '' ]]
make format    # ruff format + --fix
```

Run one test: `uv run --no-sync pytest tests/test_x.py::test_name -q`.

## Conventions & gotchas

- **Versioning is git-tag-derived** (`hatch-vcs`). Never hand-edit a version; `src/[[ package_name ]]/_version.py` is generated (gitignored). Tag `vX.Y.Z` to release.
- **`src/` layout, `py.typed`, Pydantic v2, `structlog`.** Ruff line-length 120; keep it clean (`make lint`) before committing.
[% if has_server %]- **Any endpoint that does something is a boundary.** There's no auth by default — treat reaching the port as host access. Gate state-changing routes behind the shared read-only / origin guards, and fence any caller-supplied path under a configured root.
[% endif %]- Wire schemas (if any) are checked in and verified in CI — regenerate and commit when the types change, don't let the committed copy drift.

## CI / release

CI runs via the shared [`argus-ci`](https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/argus-ci) reusable workflow. Release publishes to PyPI (OIDC trusted publishing) + GHCR on `v*` tags. Run `copier update` to pull template (CI/release/tooling) changes.
